# Backend architecture rules

- Use ASP.NET Core Web API with C#.
- Use Controller, Service, Repository, DTO, Entity, and Data/DbContext layers.
- Controllers depend on service interfaces; services depend on repository interfaces; repositories depend on DbContext.
- Register dependencies through built-in Dependency Injection.
- Keep business logic in services, persistence in repositories, and HTTP concerns in controllers.
- Keep entities under `Models/Entities`; DTOs under `DTOs`; DbContext and EF configurations under `Data`.
- Do not return EF entities from API endpoints.
- Use AutoMapper profiles for Entity ↔ DTO mapping; explicitly exclude secrets/internal fields.
- Use async I/O and propagate `CancellationToken`.
- Avoid unnecessary abstraction, duplicated logic, static mutable state, and service locator patterns.
- Use nullable reference types and clear naming.
- Keep API contracts stable and document changes.
